Gaokao-Bench Changelog
======================

Versioning
----------
- Engine versions track the harness, scorer, CLI, packaging, and release tools.
- Dataset versions track questions, answers, points, assets, and manifest policy.
- A published result must record both versions plus the dataset and protocol hashes.

2026-11-10
----------
Engine 0.1.2 / Dataset 0.0.3

- License dataset 0.0.3 as a whole under CC BY 4.0, including question text,
  answers, figures, selection, schema, and scoring metadata; the code and
  harness remain Apache-2.0.
- Publish Hugging Face dataset metadata with license cc-by-4.0 and retain source
  attribution in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
- Keep public_ranking_allowed=true with attribution and exact revision pinning.
- Treat public redistribution as cleared with attribution for 0.0.3 and later.

2026-11-10
----------
Engine 0.1.1 / Dataset 0.0.2

- Dataset 0.0.2 is a metadata-only update to 0.0.1. Questions, answers, points,
  and figure crops are unchanged.
- Set public_ranking_allowed=true for dataset 0.0.2. Third parties may publish
  leaderboards, comparative rankings, and model evaluation results when they cite
  the exact dataset revision and evaluation protocol.
- Keep exam_material_license=NOASSERTION. Permission to rank model results does
  not relicense the underlying exam text, figures, or third-party material.
- Dataset 0.0.1 remains immutable and keeps its historical
  public_ranking_allowed=false manifest.
- Fix the scoring formula so the metric identifier renders correctly in KaTeX.
- Remove the engine release tip from README; release history is maintained here.

2026-11-10
----------
Engine 0.1.0 / Dataset 0.0.1

- Split the subject-neutral Engine from versioned Benchmark Specs and immutable
  data packages.
- Add scoped point-weighted metrics, text/vision slices, provider routing records,
  failure usage accounting, progress events, resume, and retry-failed.
- Fix set-builder interval false negatives in the deterministic scorer.
- Add the all-subject construction, validator, evidence-level, and versioning
  architecture in ARCHITECTURE.md.

2026-11-09
----------
Dataset 0.0.1

- Publish the 2025 Gaokao Mathematics objective baseline: five papers, 74 scored
  questions, 353 official points, and four figure-required questions.
- Add deterministic all-or-nothing scoring, text and vision profiles, gold/empty/
  malformed examples, and immutable file hashes.
